I don't intend to re-open the whole discussions from the past,
just one point; the crucial factor is that you have no sufficient
HP buffer that you build up otherwise. Having HPs is - beside the
lucky finds and lucky RNG events I mentioned - what makes your
character survive. Not having that will kill you from the many
sources the early game provides, starting from traps, continuing
with missiles from monsters, to name just two factors that you
encounter, and especially in the mines where a PR will strive to.
You also have to rely on your pet; a dead pet (traps, monsters)
or a lost pet (traps) will instantly make you a piece of cake for
the critters populating the dungeons and mines.

Typically PR proponents don't need to mind, because they can quickly
start another game and forget the spoiled one. But if one wants to
increase survival probability in the most critical phase of the game
it's an extremely bad strategy.

YMMV, of course.

